## Data layer

{{BACKEND}} is the source of truth. Local storage is a cache, never the record.

- Every table has row-level security / access rules enabled. No exceptions.
- Migrations live in version control and are applied forward only.
- Models are immutable, with `copyWith` and value equality (`freezed`, or
  hand-written `==` / `hashCode`).

## Non-negotiable rules

- ❌ No API keys, tokens or secrets in source. Not in `lib/`, not in
  `android/`, not in `ios/`. Use `--dart-define`, `--dart-define-from-file`, or
  a backend.
- ❌ Auth tokens go in {{SECURE_STORAGE}}, never in `shared_preferences`.
  `shared_preferences` is plain text on disk.
- ❌ Never commit `android/key.properties`, `*.keystore`, `*.jks`,
  `google-services.json` or `GoogleService-Info.plist`. A leaked upload key ends
  your ability to ship updates under that package name.
- ❌ No `print()` in `lib/`. Use a logger, or `debugPrint` guarded by `kDebugMode`.
- ❌ No new dependency without asking. Every package is app size and supply-chain
  risk, and Flutter's tree-shaking cannot remove a package you imported.
- ❌ No `// ignore:` without a comment on the same line explaining why.
{{DOMAIN_RULES}}
- ✅ Thumb-first: every primary action reachable one-handed, tap targets ≥ 48dp
  (Material) / 44pt (Cupertino).
- ✅ `Semantics` labels on every interactive element, localized like any other
  string.
- ✅ Haptic feedback on destructive and confirming actions, not on every tap.

## Commit cadence

- Messages in English, `type(scope): description` (conventional commits).
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `style`, `perf`.
- One commit = one complete logical change. Never commit a tree that does not
  compile.
- Never `--no-verify`. If a gate fails, fix the code, not the gate.

## Quality gates

- `dart format --set-exit-if-changed` — clean
- `flutter analyze --fatal-infos --fatal-warnings` — zero issues
- `flutter test` — green
- Before push: the pre-push plan for the active profile
- Before a release build: `preflight` equivalent + manual Golden Paths +
  `flutter-doctor` with zero FAILs

The gates are declared in `.githooks/lib/gates.def` and executed by
`.githooks/lib/quality.sh` (Git Bash), `quality.ps1` (PowerShell) and
`quality.cmd` (cmd.exe) — the same plan in all three.

**Never weaken a gate to make it pass.** If a check is wrong, fix the check in
the same commit and say why. If the code is wrong, fix the code.

